{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-18963","model_call":26,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1732"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1732"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_131466386#6_267977682","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1732","rank":4,"snippet":"Newsmax guest calls out network for 'lying to its own viewers' live on Newsmax Live from Newsmax, it's ... a call-out! David Litt, former speechwriter for former President Barack Obama, called out Newsmax on Monday for pushing false claims about the 2020 presidential election — while live on Newsmax. He unexpectedly got his dig in during a segment where he was asked to talk about Elon Musk hosting Saturday Night Live over the weekend. \" What happened on SNL this weekend was that people made stuff up and then said it on television like it's true,\" Litt said. \" And that actually happens pretty frequently in American TV. For example, in 2020, <cover>Dominion Voting Systems sued Newsmax over its false claims about election fraud. </cover>Newsmax was lying to its own viewers, and Newsmax had to settle that lawsuit.\" In April, Newsmax apologized to an employee of Dominion Voting Systems about its false claims about the 2020 presidential election and reportedly settled a defamation lawsuit. \"\" , \"start_char\": 6369.000000 , \"title\": \"\" , \"url\": \"https://news.yahoo.com/hug-just-doctor-ordered-york-162444455.html\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_52_1210906276#4_2410424879","rank":3,"relevance":3}]},"time":12},"model_calls":26,"document_judgments":25,"relevance_3":16,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
